    <string name="setup_note_webde">For Web.de, “POP3/IMAP” must be enabled once (Web.de mailbox → Settings → POP3/IMAP access). After that your normal password is enough; with two-factor protection you need an app password.</string>
    <string name="setup_note_gmx">For GMX, “POP3/IMAP” must be enabled once (GMX mailbox → Email → Settings → POP3/IMAP access). After that your normal password is enough; with two-factor protection you need an app password.</string>
    <string name="setup_note_outlook">With two-factor protection you need an app password (link below). Note: some company accounts (Microsoft 365) don\'t allow password sign-in — the connection will then fail.</string>
    <string name="setup_note_yahoo">Yahoo requires an app password: create it via the link below (Account security → App passwords) and paste it here.</string>
    <string name="setup_note_tonline">T-Online needs its own “email password” (not your customer-center password). You set it in the Email Center under “Passwords”.</string>
    <string name="setup_note_icloud">Apple requires an app-specific password: create it at appleid.apple.com under “Sign-In and Security”.</string>
